MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Something like this normally is due to permission issues or environment settings. When you say "I have Rscript available on all the nodes" you should also make sure that that is true for all users, but this line

Added /opt/hadoop/R/bin to PATH in ~/.bash_profile file

is obviously user specific. What happens is that mapreduce jobs run usually as a special hadoop user for which ~ expands to a different path. Our scripts operate directly on /etc/profile, but there may be other ways to achieve the same result. I hope this helps

Antonio

